 success←GitHub_SSH_OK;cmd;r;tfn;Found
⍝ 1 if SSH authentication to GitHub works right now, 0 if GitHub refused the key.\\
⍝ Does not get stuck on "Enter passphrase" but would return a 0.\\
⍝ Anything that prevents an answer - no network, no SSH, a timeout - is signalled rather than
⍝ returned as a 0: "your key is not accepted" and "GitHub could not be reached" are different
⍝ problems, and a caller that gets a 0 for both can only guess.\\
⍝ Note that <ssh -T git@github.com> exits with 1 even when it worked, so the exit code says
⍝ nothing and only the greeting does. On Unix a non-zero exit makes ⎕SH signal, which is why the
⍝ output is collected in a file rather than taken from the result of ⎕SH.
 Found←{∨/∨/¨(⍺∘⍷)¨⊆⍵}
 tfn←F.GetTempFilename2'APLGit2_ssh'
 cmd←'ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 '
 cmd,←'-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -T git@github.com >"',tfn,'" 2>&1'
 :Trap 0
     {}⎕SH cmd
 :EndTrap
 r←{22::'' ⋄ ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1}tfn
 F.DeleteFile tfn
 success←'successfully authenticated'Found r
 :If ~success
 :AndIf ~'Permission denied'Found r                  ⍝ Then it is not an authentication problem
     ('Cannot tell whether SSH to GitHub works: ',{0=≢∊⍵:'SSH said nothing at all' ⋄ ⊃{⍺,' ',⍵}/⊆⍵}r)Assert 0
 :EndIf
⍝Done
